# SRG-APP-000211-WSR-000129  -  CAT II
# The web server must separate the hosted applications from hosted web
# server management functionality.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000211-WSR-000129
group:           V-206395
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-001082
control_rev5:    SC-2

contribution:    Splunk Enterprise separates the management surface from the application
                 surface in two ways the product itself controls: splunkd's management and
                 REST interface listens on its own port with its own source address list
                 and is reached by Splunk Web over the loopback address, and the
                 capabilities that constitute management (admin_all_objects, edit_server,
                 edit_web_settings, indexes_edit, install_apps) are withheld from the
                 built-in non-administrative roles. Because a capability can only be
                 granted - "enabled" is the only accepted value - withholding one is
                 checked by its absence from a role stanza.

governs:         authorize.conf - Used to create roles.
governs:         server.conf - Core server settings, including the certificates and protocols used to
                 protect management and replication traffic.
governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           server.conf [httpServer] acceptFrom non_empty
check:           server.conf [httpServer] acceptFrom not_equals *
check:           web.conf [settings] mgmtHostPort matches ^(localhost|127\.0\.0\.1|\[::1\]):[0-9]+$
check:           authorize.conf [role_user] admin_all_objects absent
check:           authorize.conf [role_power] admin_all_objects absent
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          server.conf [httpServer] acceptFrom https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/server.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] mgmtHostPort https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Network segmentation or firewall rules that keep the management port off
                 the user network - network component configuration
external:        Review of locally defined roles beyond the built-in user and power roles,
                 to confirm management capabilities are held only by administrative roles -
                 organizational role design, which configuration alone cannot classify as
                 administrative or not
external:        Separation of management and application functions in any custom app's own
                 endpoints - application development

citation:        server.conf.spec:1291 ([httpServer]) with :1345-1360 (acceptFrom, default
                 "*" accept from anywhere); web.conf.spec:35-41 (mgmtHostPort, the IP
                 address and port where Splunk Web looks for splunkd);
                 authorize.conf.spec:67-72 ([role_<roleName>], <capability> = <enabled>,
                 "'enabled' is the only accepted value here, as capabilities are disabled
                 by default"); authorize.conf.spec:447-452
                 ([capability::admin_all_objects], lets a user bypass any Access Control
                 List restriction); authorize.conf.spec:665 ([capability::edit_server]),
                 :733 ([capability::edit_web_settings]), :753 ([capability::indexes_edit]),
                 :760 ([capability::install_apps])
finding:         The application does not separate management from hosted application
                 functionality to the extent the product allows: the splunkd management
                 listener accepts connections from any source, Splunk Web reaches splunkd
                 over a non-loopback address, or a built-in non-administrative role has
                 been granted a management capability.
